# Copy this file to .env.agent and set the values below.
# See SETUP.md for the rationale.

# Absolute path to the primary copy of the base standard — the edition
# declared in context/00-normative-base.md. Every step that grounds a
# claim against MPEG-DASH reads this file, and bin/check-normative-base.py
# refuses to start a build without it.
#
# It is a licensed single-user document, so it is not in this repository
# and its location is a property of your checkout, not of the project.
# Obtain it from the ISO catalogue link in context/00-normative-base.md;
# the sha256 declared there is what identifies it, so a different file at
# this path is detected rather than used.
#
# For a single run this can be overridden with the SGAI_NORMATIVE_PDF
# environment variable; the check announces the override every time it
# takes effect.
NORMATIVE_PDF_PATH=

# Stage 5 — GitHub issues pipeline.
# Comma-separated list of GitHub usernames whose issues the pipeline
# can process and respond to end-to-end automatically. Issues from
# outsiders (anyone NOT in this list) still get triaged + drafted, but
# the response is held with label `ai-needs-review` and Nicolas
# decides manually whether to post it (and optionally promote the
# author into TRUSTED_GH_USERS).
TRUSTED_GH_USERS=nicolaslevy,emilsas
